# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# .env.local is gitignored — never commit real secrets.

# ── Gmail (for "Send to client" email) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a Google App Password (not your normal Gmail password):
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
GMAIL_USER=your.gmail@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx

# ── WhatsApp self-hosted Cloud API (whatsapp-server-shivani on Fly) ──────────
# AiSensy was fully decommissioned 2026-05-15 — fm-coach now talks to the
# self-hosted WA Cloud API server for both outbound (templates + free-text)
# and inbound (HMAC-verified webhook → /api/whatsapp-webhook here).
#
# WHATSAPP_SERVER_URL points at the Fly app, WHATSAPP_SERVER_API_KEY is the
# shared bearer token (also set on the WA server as ADMIN_API_KEY). The
# webhook secret is set on the WA server as FM_COACH_WEBHOOK_SECRET and
# must match the WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_SECRET we verify inbound with.
WHATSAPP_SERVER_URL=https://whatsapp-server-shivani.fly.dev
WHATSAPP_SERVER_API_KEY=your_shared_admin_token
WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_shared_webhook_secret

# ── Recipe inbox (forward reels/photos/PDFs to the coach WhatsApp number) ─────
# Comma-separated phone numbers (the coach's PERSONAL phone(s), matched on the
# last 10 digits). Every inbound WhatsApp message from these numbers is staged
# as a recipe candidate in ~/fm-plans/_recipe_inbox/ for review at /recipes —
# never saved as a client note. The webhook runs on the Fly app, so set this
# there too: flyctl secrets set RECIPE_INBOX_NUMBERS=919876543210 -a theochretree-coach
# RECIPE_INBOX_NUMBERS=919876543210

# ── Coach notification phone (for cal.com booking alerts via WhatsApp) ─────────
# Your own WhatsApp number in E.164 format. Used by coach_booking_alert_v1 to
# send you an instant WhatsApp whenever a cal.com booking is created / rescheduled
# / cancelled. Falls back to GMAIL_USER email if this is not set.
COACH_NOTIFY_PHONE=+919876543210

# ── Path overrides (optional — defaults shown) ────────────────────────────────
# FMDB_PLANS_DIR=/home/youruser/fm-plans
# FMDB_CATALOGUE_DIR=/path/to/fm-database/data
# FMDB_RESOURCES_DIR=/home/youruser/fm-resources

# ── Public base URL (for canonical links in emails etc.) ──────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3002

# Authorize API-spending shims (set to 1 in the app; chat shells omit it).
FM_API_OK=1

# ── Revenue export → ochre-funnel (growth-system Loop 1) ──────────────────────
# fm-coach POSTs payment / programme_completed / active_client_count events to
# the marketing app so funnels are judged on LTV, not just tickets, and ads
# pause when the coach is at capacity. Contract: docs/REVENUE_EXPORT_CONTRACT.md
# Unset → every emit is a silent no-op (the outbox still records for backfill).
# OCHRE_FUNNEL_REVENUE_URL=https://ochre-funnel.fly.dev/api/webhooks/fm-coach-revenue
# FM_REVENUE_EXPORT_SECRET=shared_hmac_secret_same_as_ochre_funnel_FM_COACH_REVENUE_SECRET
# Capacity config travels IN the events (the coach owns her cap).
# The practice holds 100 active clients; the weekly throttle is 20 NEW
# SIGNUPS (trailing 7 days) — that's what gates lead-buying.
# FM_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS=100
# FM_MAX_SIGNUPS_PER_WEEK=20
# FM_DISCOVERY_CALLS_PER_WEEK=8

# The address CLIENTS see on email from the app. Optional.
#
# Gmail authenticates as GMAIL_USER but will send as any address that account
# has verified under Settings -> Accounts -> "Send mail as". Set this to the
# practice address so a client is not receiving notes about their programme
# from an operations mailbox they have never seen.
#
# If the address is a verified alias of GMAIL_USER, this is all you need.
# If it is a separate Google Workspace account, point GMAIL_USER and
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD at that account instead and leave this unset.
#
# Internal alerts (cron digests, integrity warnings) deliberately ignore this.
# GMAIL_FROM=shivani@theochretree.com   # only if it is a verified alias

# Client-facing email sends from the coach's own Workspace account when these
# are set; automated mail keeps using GMAIL_USER above. Separate accounts, so
# this needs its own App Password (Google Account -> Security -> 2-Step
# Verification -> App passwords). Both required; one without the other falls
# back to the ops mailbox.
COACH_GMAIL_USER=shivani@theochretree.com
COACH_GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# ── Remote access to the coach UI (cloudflared → fmcoach.shivanihari.com) ───
#
# ⚠ READ BEFORE STARTING THE TUNNEL. The coach UI has FOUR auth modes
# (see src/proxy.ts). On the Mac it runs in mode 3, LOCAL DEV — a NO-OP,
# because FLY_INTAKE_ONLY is Fly-only and these two were never set locally.
# localhost:3002 therefore has NO authentication at all.
#
# That is fine while it is only reachable on the LAN. Put a public tunnel in
# front of it without setting these and you publish the whole dashboard —
# every client's records — to anyone who has the URL.
#
# Set BOTH, then `pm2 delete fm-coach && pm2 start ecosystem.config.js`
# (a plain `pm2 restart` does NOT re-read this file), then confirm the wall
# is really up BEFORE exposing anything:
#
#     curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://localhost:3002/clients-v2
#
# It must print 401. If it prints 200 the password did not load — stop, and do
# not start the tunnel. Full runbook: docs/COACH_REMOTE_ACCESS.md
#
# Username defaults to "shivani" when only the password is set. The public
# client routes (/intake/, /s/, /letter/, /app/ …) bypass this wall by design,
# so clients are unaffected.
# COACH_AUTH_USERNAME=shivani
# COACH_AUTH_PASSWORD=

# The phone-shaped coach surface (/m) uses a signed session cookie instead of
# Basic auth — iOS PWAs re-prompt badly on Basic. Unset → /m is just another
# coach route (404 on Fly). Fails closed.
# COACH_MOBILE_PASSWORD=

# Public origin of the coach UI, used for links in cron digest emails the
# coach opens on her phone. NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL (that is the Fly intake
# host, which 404s coach routes) and NOT localhost (cron's internal calls).
# Falls back to APP_URL, then http://localhost:3002.
# COACH_PUBLIC_URL=https://fmcoach.shivanihari.com

# ── Infra watchdog + phone→Mac bridge ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# Watchdog: /api/cron/infra-health runs every 5 min, probes the public tunnel
# and the auth wall in front of it, RESTARTS the tunnel when it is down, and
# emails only after ~15 min of failed repairs (or at once if coach routes are
# being served publicly with no auth). Disabled entirely when COACH_PUBLIC_URL
# is unset. It needs one sudoers line to actually repair — see
# docs/COACH_REMOTE_ACCESS.md.
# COACH_TUNNEL_SERVICE=com.cloudflare.cloudflared   # launchd label; this is the default
# COACH_DIGEST_EMAIL=                                # where alerts go; defaults to GMAIL_USER

# Bridge: lets /m on Fly perform the few actions that must WRITE the
# authoritative client.yaml — currently issuing an intake link. Both hosts need
# the same secret; unset on either side and the bridge route 404s as though it
# did not exist.
#
# ⚠ COACH_MAC_URL MUST NOT BE THE CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL. If it points at
# fmcoach.shivanihari.com the bridge dies with the tunnel — and a dead tunnel is
# the exact outage this exists to survive. Use the Tailscale address of the
# mini, or another private path that fails independently.
# COACH_MAC_URL=http://100.x.y.z:3002
# COACH_BRIDGE_SECRET=
